he centuries these Americans have stood  up to defend our country often at great  personal sacrifice for themselves and  their families I am honored to be  counted among the ranks there are 23  million veterans alive today in the u.s.  how best can we honor and celebrate them  for my part I wish to honor the veterans  who came before me who have worked to  improve the perception of soldiers  returning from war in Iraq I was  overwhelmed with the generosity and  support of the American people my  soldiers receive packages of  heartwarming cards from people we had  never met returning at the airport we  were given hugs and Cheers  I know that in large part this is from  the efforts of veterans who came before  us who fought different Wars and had  very different treatment upon return I'm  grateful to those who came before us who  work to ensure that people are separate  from politics and that soldiers  returning for more regarded as heroes  how else can we honor and celebrate my  suggestion is that one wonderful thing  you can do today to honor veterans is to  employ embody their values in your own  life I encourage you to think about what  can be learned about the values that  veterans live by about being part of  something bigger than yourself in a  military you take the time to make sure  the soldier next to you knows how to  shoot a weapon or inspect a vehicle or  how to operate a radio unity development  shared mission yes but also we take the  time because in the most literal of ways  we never know when our lives may depend  on the person next to us knowing how to  do his or her job what if we all live  like this like our lives depended on the  people next to us living up to their  potential and being equipped to fulfill  the best of themselves and contribution  to the betterment of our country and  humanity this Veterans Day I encourage  you to honor and celebrate the veterans  in your life send a package or send a  prayer to those deployed overseas are  those 